0Z","county":"Jefferson","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"1.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-05-02T17:59Z","endLat":42.94,"endLon":-88.9,"episode":214270,"id":1342852,"injuries":0,"lat":42.95,"location":"1.71 NW Ft Atkinson","lon":-88.87,"narrative":"The Rock River in the Fort Atkinson area continued to have impacts from high water. The floodwaters affected some park land and boat launchees, and partially flooded the following roads: Sinissippi Drive, Bark River Road from Kutz Road to Rock River Road and E Milwaukee Ave, and Rock River Rd from Highway 106 to the Fort Atkinson city limits.","source":"River/Stream Gage","state":"WI","type":"Flood","wfo":"MKX"},{"begin":"2026-05-01T06:00Z","county":"Jefferson","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"1.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-05-04T17:59Z","endLat":42.9,"endLon":-89.02,"episode":214270,"id":1342869,"injuries":0,"lat":42.93,"location":"2.9 NE Busseyville","lon":-88.94,"narrative":"The Rock River at Lake Koshkonong continued to have impacts from high water. Floodwaters reached Oxbow Bend Road in the area of the gauge on the east side of the lake. The following roads were flooded: the end of Road 9, end of Road 8 St, end of E Road 7, Lakeview Dr, Charley Bluff Rd north of Royce Dallman Park, parts of Lamp Rd, Willow Rd, parts of Blackhawk Island Rd. Water surrounded some structures on Lamp Rd and toward the end of Blackhawk Island Rd. Low lying areas of Lakeland Campground and Altpeter County Park flooded. There was water into yards along High Ridge Rd. Homes and docks in the Blackhawk Island area on the north side of Lake Koshkonong were affected by floodwaters.","source":"River/Stream Gage","state":"WI","type":"Flood","wfo":"MKX"},{"begin":"2026-05-01T06:38Z","county":"Gonzales","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2026-05-01T06:38Z","endLat":29.52,"endLon":-97.69,"episode":213596,"id":1338424,"injuries":0,"lat":29.52,"location":"0.6 E Belmont","lon":-97.69,"magnitude":1.0,"narrative":"A